    "turn_text": "No, no, I think you make a great point. But I think what the speaker is saying is in divided government, with something as just as broken and intentionally broken as our current you know as our borders currently uh... the uh... maybe the only way that we can actually get the democrats to to do the right thing is to pair it with something that they desperately want to set that the you know that the white house desperately want uh... and and so i think that that's just a bit just reality you know that in a divided government with the senate control by the democrats with with obviously joe biden the white house Um, this may be the one trade that makes some sense to do to secure our border because remember what Christopher Ray and we don't always, you know, you and I don't always agree with what Christopher Ray said, but he said Hamas is because of what Hamas is doing in the Middle East and this terrorist activity. Uh, he's concerned about what this means and this and this quote, inspiring other terrorists to do things here in the United States. Well, when you make that statement and you look at the situation in our border, which is wide open, a hundred and fifty People have been apprehended who were on the terrorist watch list just this year. And there was just one terrorist running around for two weeks before they finally got him inside the con. I mean, that is how serious the situation is. So I think what the speaker is saying is just a reflection of reality that we may have to look at some kind of pairing of these issues. to get done what needs to be done to protect the homeland",
